    "status": "present",
    "value": "Implement front, middle and back insertion/removal; when two middle positions exist, removal chooses the earlier one. The approach is: two deques keep left size equal to right or one larger; left back is the frontmost middle. Its target cost is O(1) expected per operation/O(n) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
